course: dictionary
lesson: 10495
title: Tusks
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A tusk is a very long, pointed tooth that grows out of the mouth of some animals. Elephants, walruses, wild boars and narwhals all have tusks.
explain: Context tells you what tusks do. «A walrus has two long tusks, and walruses use their tusks like ice picks to pull their heavy bodies out of the water onto the ice.» The words ice picks and pull tell you a tusk helps an animal climb out.
explain: Tusks are used for digging, fighting, lifting and getting food. They keep growing through the animal's life, so an old animal can have longer tusks than a young one.
fact: A tusk is a very long, pointed tooth.
fact: Tusks are used for digging, fighting, lifting and getting food.
fact: «The narwhal's tusk» grows in a spiral through the upper lip and can be up to about 3 metres long.
fact: Tusks are made of ivory. «Poachers kill elephants for their tusks», and selling ivory is banned in most countries.
fact: Tusks keep growing through the animal's life.
exercise: «The walrus uses its two long tusks to haul itself onto the ice.» What do the tusks help the walrus do? | *Pull itself out of the water onto the ice | Keep its body warm in the sun | Sing to its friends under the sea | Find clams with its tusks
exercise: Which animals in this lesson have tusks? | Dolphins and whales | Lions and tigers | Seals and sea lions | *Elephants, walruses, wild boars and narwhals
exercise: «The narwhal's tusk is a tooth that grows in a spiral.» Find and copy the word that names the long, pointed tooth. | narwhal's | spiral | *tusk | grows
test: What are tusks made of, as you learn in conservation lessons? | *Ivory | Rubber | Bone | Wood
test: Why do poachers kill elephants? | To keep the land clear for farms | To make houses from their bones | Because elephants are dangerous to people | *For their tusks
exam: «Tusks keep growing through the animal's life.» What does this tell you? | Tusks grow only in winter | *Tusks keep growing for as long as the animal is alive | Tusks stop growing after one year | Tusks only grow when the animal is a baby
